.TH SDL_AppIterate 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_AppIterate \- App-implemented iteration entry point for
.BR SDL_MAIN_USE_CALLBACKS
apps.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_main.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_AppResult SDL_AppIterate(void *appstate);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apps implement this function when using
.BR SDL_MAIN_USE_CALLBACKS \[char46]
If using a standard \(dqmain\(dq function, you should not supply this\[char46]
.PP
This function is called repeatedly by SDL after
.BR SDL_AppInit
returns
.BR SDL_APP_CONTINUE \[char46]
The function should operate as a single iteration the program\(aqs primary loop; it should update whatever state it needs and draw a new frame of video, usually\[char46]
.PP
On some platforms, this function will be called at the refresh rate of the display (which might change during the life of your app!)\[char46] There are no promises made about what frequency this function might run at\[char46] You should use SDL\(aqs timer functions if you need to see how much time has passed since the last iteration\[char46]
.PP
There is no need to process the SDL event queue during this function; SDL will send events as they arrive in
.BR SDL_AppEvent ,
and in most cases the event queue will be empty when this function runs anyhow\[char46]
.PP
This function should not go into an infinite mainloop; it should do one iteration of whatever the program does and return\[char46]
.PP
The
.BR appstate
parameter is an optional pointer provided by the app during
.BR SDL_AppInit ()\[char46]
If the app never provided a pointer, this will be NULL\[char46]
.PP
If this function returns
.BR SDL_APP_CONTINUE ,
the app will continue normal operation, receiving repeated calls to
.BR SDL_AppIterate
and
.BR SDL_AppEvent
for the life of the program\[char46] If this function returns
.BR SDL_APP_FAILURE ,
SDL will call
.BR SDL_AppQuit
and terminate the process with an exit code that reports an error to the platform\[char46] If it returns
.BR SDL_APP_SUCCESS ,
SDL calls
.BR SDL_AppQuit
and terminates with an exit code that reports success to the platform\[char46]
.PP
This function is called by SDL on the main thread\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I appstate
an optional pointer, provided by the app in
.BR SDL_AppInit \[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.BR SDL_APP_FAILURE
to terminate with an error,
.BR SDL_APP_SUCCESS
to terminate with success,
.BR SDL_APP_CONTINUE
to continue\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function may get called concurrently with
.BR SDL_AppEvent ()
for events not pushed on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_AppInit (3),
.BR SDL_AppEvent (3)
